00:00:39.499 --> 00:00:44.579
OK, so going into Avengers: Infinity War,
we need to remember that last time Captain

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:48.620
America had his shield was during his bitter
showdown with Iron Man at the end of Civil

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.620
War.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:53.520
Tony Stark, who felt betrayed that Steve Rogers
covered up the fact the Winter Soldier murdered

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.879
his parents, angrily told Steve the shield
didn't belong to him and that he didn't deserve

00:00:57.879 --> 00:00:58.879
it anymore.

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:01.690
Cap abandoned the shield and went on the run
after that.

00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.850
And I think in Infinity War, we'll see Cap
operating without a shield for a little while,

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.290
for example, he doesn't seem to have one here
when he catches Proxima Midnight's spear and

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.540
he's just using his fists against this Outrider.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:17.460
However, in that epic shot of Cap leading
the charge in Wakanda, we can see he's acquired

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.220
some cool new arm gauntlets which are a big
clue to his new shield.

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:25.110
The colour and style of Cap's new arm shields
and the fact they have what look like claws

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.810
on them indicate they're some cool tech made
in Wakanda.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:33.410
In fact, unlike the MCU where it's Tony's
father Howard Stark who made Cap's shield,

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:37.550
in a number of Marvel comics, it's actually
Black Panther who provides Cap with his shield.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:41.940
But, although it's T'Challa who says the awesome
line, "get this man a shield" in Infinity

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.900
War, I think it will be his sister, Shuri,
who will be the person responsible for Cap's

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:46.900
new arm-shields.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.210
Why do I think this?

00:01:48.210 --> 00:01:52.410
Well, because she's a genius who's spent many
years researching vibranium and developing

00:01:52.410 --> 00:01:56.940
technology, and Kevin Feige said, 'she runs
the entire Wakandan design group'.

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:01.360
Also, if you look back at the Black Panther
trailers, you'll see Shuri sporting some pretty

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:06.100
fierce vibranium-based weaponry on her own
arms in the form of two Panther-style blasters

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.390
that she developed herself.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:12.749
In fact, I wonder if that smart Wakandan tech
we see on Cap's arms could make a shield materialise

00:02:12.749 --> 00:02:17.799
in a similar way to how Black Panther's suit
appears here in his first solo film, or similar

00:02:17.799 --> 00:02:21.480
to the hard-light shielding we've seen Black
Panther use in the comics.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.159
If this happens it wouldn't be the first time
we've seen an energy shield on screen in one

00:02:25.159 --> 00:02:26.510
of Marvel's properties.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:31.400
In the TV show Agents of SHIELD, Coulson can
activate an energy shield using his prosthetic

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:35.870
hand, and in the animation Next Avengers:
Heroes of Tomorrow, Captain America and Black

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:39.719
Widow's son, James Rogers, used an energy
shield designed by Tony Stark.

00:02:39.719 --> 00:02:44.489
As for Cap himself, he's used various energy
shields in the comics.

00:02:44.489 --> 00:02:49.099
In the mid-90s, Sharon Carter gave him an
experimental plasma shield which was activated

00:02:49.099 --> 00:02:52.069
from his wrist and which could repel small
arms fire.

00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:55.950
A couple of years later in the comics, Carter
gave Rogers a glove which could project a

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.499
photon force field.

00:02:57.499 --> 00:03:01.909
This photonic shield simulated a vibranium
matrix, so that it could store and deflect

00:03:01.909 --> 00:03:03.730
energy back to an enemy.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:08.239
In other versions, as well as defensive properties,
the shield also offered possibilities for

00:03:08.239 --> 00:03:09.239
attack.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:13.379
And it's been able to fire energy blasts as
well as transform into weapons.

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:17.029
One of the cool things we've seen on screen
is how Cap has thrown his shield around, using

00:03:17.029 --> 00:03:18.969
magnetic elements to call it back.

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:23.329
We might not get that from a new shield, but
in the comics, later versions, such as the

00:03:23.329 --> 00:03:28.700
zero point energy shield, can be thrown at
an enemy and then upon impact they disintegrate.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:32.739
And then a new shield can be created from
the energy generator in a matter of seconds.

00:03:32.739 --> 00:03:36.590
I hope we do still get to see a version of
Cap's shield that he can throw as it's given

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:40.209
us some memorable moments so far in the MCU.

00:03:40.209 --> 00:03:44.029
The look of Cap's gauntlets in the trailer
also makes me think of the Captain America:

00:03:44.029 --> 00:03:45.519
Steve Rogers series.

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:49.669
In those comic books, Cap has a triangular
shield, which can be split into two parts

00:03:49.669 --> 00:03:53.889
so he can attack a baddie with one half and
still protect himself with the other, and

00:03:53.889 --> 00:03:57.439
it also has an energy blade which can be used
to cut through things.

00:03:57.439 --> 00:04:01.819
So, why do I think this could be the basis
for Cap's new shield in Infinity War?

00:04:01.819 --> 00:04:06.489
Well, if you look closely at this epic team
shot in Wakanda, you can see that Cap's gauntlets

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:10.889
have a triangular shape to them and there
are also several claws, which could be used

00:04:10.889 --> 00:04:13.019
for cutting, like in the comics.

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:18.060
And given he's got two arm gauntlets, and
he's in Wakanda, the home of all things super-high-tech,

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:22.580
this makes me think that those two objects
on his arms could likely transform into a

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:23.580
shield.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.150
A possible wrinkle in this theory is that
in Spider-Man: Homecoming, when Happy Hogan

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:32.160
was arranging the move of tech from the Avengers
Tower, he mentioned a prototype of Captain

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.160
America's new shield.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.160
I still think that Cap's new arm shields do
look Wakandan.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.620
So, I wonder if the new shield that Tony made
will actually end up in the hands of Bucky

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.930
Barnes either in Infinity War or in Avengers
4.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:47.889
In the comics, Bucky does take on the mantle
of Captain America and there was already a

00:04:47.889 --> 00:04:52.091
nod to that when the Winter Soldier caught
Cap's shield in the second Captain America

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.530
solo movie.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:57.930
If you've seen my Infinity War trailer breakdown
video, then you'll know that we see Tony Stark

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.889
holding a small phone that looks like the
same one Cap had FedExed to him at the end

00:05:01.889 --> 00:05:02.919
of Civil War.

00:05:02.919 --> 00:05:06.760
Which means we'll very likely see a reunion
between Tony and Steve at some point in Infinity

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.630
War or Avengers 4.

